{{Spoilers}}

There are four secrets that are unlocked by performing various feats in the game. Once unlocked, you can visit the secret areas indefinitely from the [[Portal]] screen. Usually, the secret areas offer a quest chain with three tasks each, requiring resources from varying levels of [[Mining]] and [[Fishing]]. '''Completing these quests awards permanent bonuses. Secrets should not be seen as optional because they give huge bonuses to the progression of the game.'''

At level 40 [[Smithing]], you're able to craft Enigmatic Boosters which improve Secret bonuses by +2% per level.

The civilization secret is the check boxes found throughout the game. There are 10 empty circles around the Secrets portal. It should be noted some of the check boxes are hard to click and need to be clicked off to a side or even a little below. Also check boxes can be unmarked (Training check box) by accident. Also you need access to Fisherman's Folly Secret to complete these check boxes. See screen shots in the Civilization section for locations.

== Death's Son ==
[[File:Deaths_son.png|50px|right|Death's Son]]
When you die in [[Fight]]ing or [[Raids]], you are met by Death who has 10M health points.
<div class="mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" style="width:100%;min-height:100px;background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.1);" data-expandtext="Show solution" data-collapsetext="Hide solution">
<div class="mw-collapsible-content" style="">
Idle attacks do not work, so you have about 10 seconds to defeat Death with only your active skills. Once you've killed Death, you're transferred to Death's throne room, where you meet Death's orphaned son. When you click on the child to attempt to console it, you'll be asked to do the following:
# Collect 25 Medium Yellow Fish. Requires level 12 [[fishing]].
# Collect 10 Blue Shark. Requires level 24 [[fishing]].
# Collect 5 Hammerhead Shark. Requires level 56 [[fishing]].
After completing these quests, you find you were unable to properly console the orphan but are awarded a blessing.</div>
</div>

Finishing this secret gives +30% more kills when defeating monsters.

== Defiled Pig's Head ==
[[File:Pig_head.png|50px|right|Pig's Head on a Stake]]
In the [[Smithing]] screen, after reaching level 20 [[Smithing]], clicking on the Blacksmith prompts you to find a pill for his fever.
<div class="mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" style="width:100%;min-height:100px;background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.1);" data-expandtext="Show solution" data-collapsetext="Hide solution">
<div class="mw-collapsible-content" style="">At level 20 in [[Smithing]], you gain access to a recipe to craft Blacksmith's Pills. You only need one, but also need level 36 [[Fishing]] to gather the necessary materials (You can also slide the pill from the selection screen to the blacksmith to give it to him without crafting it). Once you've made the pill, drag it over to the Blacksmith and you'll enter his fever dream about a pig head that's been defiled on a stake. Surprisingly, even in death, the pig has final wishes that you're tasked with completing:
# Collect 99 Effluvium Ore. Requires level 30 [[mining]].
# Collect 3,000 Dubloonium Ore. Requires level 50 [[mining]].
# Collect 10 Dollar Fish. Requires level 60 [[fishing]].
Fulfill the last requests of the dead pig to finish this secret</div>
</div>
Finishing this secret will award you with +40% more AP on every [[Ascension]].

== Fisherman's Folly ==
[[File:Grammophone.png|50px|right|Grammophone]]
'''This secret cannot be completed until you reached the Blacksmith's fever dream.'''
The fisherman on the Fishing Docks can be seen swinging his legs to some unheard tune. As it turns out, he used to own a Gramophone that has since been broken, its pieces lost throughout the game.
<div class="mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" style="width:100%;min-height:100px;background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.1);" data-expandtext="Show solution" data-collapsetext="Hide solution">
<div class="mw-collapsible-content" style="">
* One piece can be found floating in the Fishing Docks, on the right side of the screen between the display for fish caught and your crafting levels.
* Another piece is found by chance in the Strength Mountain [[train]]ing area. Increasing your skiller's speed helps improve the chances of the part spawning.
* The last piece is found on the ground in the Blacksmith's fevered dream in the second secret area.
Once you've collected all the pieces, head back to the Fishing Docks to reassemble the Gramophone. Clicking on it now plays music which will attract a rather large "fish", but it will only show itself once you've caught a Dollar Fish and clicked on it (while it's on the hook) (you can click anywhere on the screen), which requires level 60 [[Fishing]]. When clicked, the screen shakes and a giant "fish" will leap out of the water, swallowing you. The screen will fade to black and you'll discovered that the large fish has swallowed the fisherman, injuring him in the process. You're now tasked with finding resources to help the man recover:[[File:Fisherman.png|right|Wounded Fisherman]]
# Collect 1,000,000 Effluvium Ore. Requires level 30 [[mining]].
# Collect 9,000,000 Copper Ore. Requires level 1 [[mining]].
# Collect 1,000,000 Old Boots. Requires level 1 [[fishing]].
As it turns out, even after helping the dying man, he isn't able to recover from the gaping hole in his chest. Nevertheless, he's grateful and grants you a blessing.</div>
</div>
Finishing this secret gives award you +50% more fishing EXP while offline and also +50% more fish caught. (this can be increased by a Smithing upgrade in the "Virtuo" tier).

==Civilization==
'''This secret cannot be completed until you've entered the Blacksmith's fever dream, Death's son's secret, and entered the fish in the Fisherman's Folly secret, and should be completed as soon as possible as its bonus increases slowly after being finished.'''
<div class="mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" style="width:100%;min-height:100px;background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.1);" data-expandtext="Show solution" data-collapsetext="Hide solution">&nbsp;
<div class="mw-collapsible-content" style="">On the [[Portal]] screen, there are ten empty placeholders for small orbs that are found by clicking hidden squares across the game. You need to click on the square until an X appears. Don't click it again after that, because you might toggle it back off. The following slideshow provides locations for each orb in the order shown above the portal:

<gallery type="slideshow" position="center" widths="600" hideaddbutton="true">
Secret4cyan.gif|Cyan: Found behind the bottom right window that provides details on a selected boss in [[Raids]]
Secret4green.gif|Green: Found on the middle right part of the Pig's Head Secret screen, in front of a palm tree leaf
Secret4yellow.gif|Yellow: Found behind a boss's thumbnail image on the top left of any Raid boss battle screen.
Secret4orange.gif|Orange: Found on the Gym [[Train]]ing screen, behind the top of the red attack dojo icon. Click the right white semicircle to hide the icon
Secret4red.gif|Red: Found on the top right corner of the [[Train]]ing Help screen
Secret4navy.gif|Navy: Found on the lobby screen when starting the game, on the middle right side of the news window
Secret4purple.gif|Purple: Found behind the top right corner of the Midas skill perk in the Green [[Perks]] screen
Secret4pink.gif|Pink: Found behind the flesh on the top right part of the Fisherman's secret screen
Secret4white.gif|White: Found on top of Death's chair in Death's secret screen
Secret4black.gif|Black: Found underneath the left part of the [[Contracts]] podium on the left side of the screen
</gallery>

[[File:Secret4.png|right]]
Click all locations to finish the secret.
</div>
</div>

After finishing this secret the [[Portal]] will now display the fourth secret screen which depicts a growing civilization. The growth of the civilization depends on "total playing time" which begins with the length of the current Ascension when unlocked plus all additional playing time afterward. Ascending after unlocking this secret will not reset the "total playing time". The usage of time candy doesn't increase the total playing time.
